---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Latent Workspace"
  description="About the Latent Workspace research notebook."
>
  <section class="about-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>A research notebook before it is a blog.</h1>
    <p>
      Latent Workspace is a public-facing study space for reading LLM and LLM-agent
      research through three priorities: interpretability, agent architecture, and safety.
    </p>
    <p>
      The goal is not to summarize papers quickly. The goal is to separate claims,
      methods, evidence, limitations, and follow-up experiments, then connect them
      into a knowledge graph that can guide future agent research.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reproduction is treated as a spectrum: code inspection, local smoke tests,
      toy approximations, partial reproduction on open models, and full reproduction
      only when the required model access and compute are realistic.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each research topic is developed through distinct formats: an evidence-led
      study note, a source-code walkthrough when implementation is public, and a
      commentary whose interpretations are kept separate from the paper's claims.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
